; Josh 18:16 ; Josh 18:18 ; Josh 18:19 (all P ). \\ \\ b. opposite side (s) , that is, of door or entrance, of tabernacle-court Exod 27:14 ; Exod 27:15 = Exod 38:14 ; Exod 38:15 (all P ), of temple 1Kgs 6:8 ; 1Kgs 7:39 (3 t. in verse) = 2Chr 4:10 ; 2Kgs 11:11 (twice in verse) = 2Chr 23:10 (twice in verse); compare Ezek 40:18 ; Ezek 40:40 (twice in verse); Ezek 40:41 ; Ezek 40:44 (twice in verse); Ezek 41:2 ; Ezek 41:26 ; Ezek 46:19 ; Ezek 47:1 ; Ezek 47:2 . 3. supports of the bases for the lavers beside the temple 1Kgs 7:30 (twice in verse); 1Kgs 7:34 (twice in verse).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4254')\">BDB4254</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3802')\">H3802</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4253')\">BDB4253</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4255')\">BDB4255</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>כָּתֵף</bdbheb> <b>noun feminine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Exod 27:15\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(2,27,15)\">Exod 27:15</ref></sup> <highlightword>shoulder, shoulder-blade, side</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; Aramaic <bdbarc>כַּתְפָּא</bdbarc>, <placeholder2692/> Arabic <placeholder2693/>); — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>כ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Zech 7:11\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(38,7,11)\">Zech 7:11</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>כֶּתֶף</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 6:8\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(11,6,8)\">1Kgs 6:8</ref> +, app. <bdbheb>כָּתֵף</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 11:14\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(23,11,14)\">Isa 11:14</ref> (but regard as apposition, or read <bdbheb>כֶּתֶף</bdbheb>); suffix <bdbheb>כְּתֵפִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 31:22\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(18,31,22)\">Job 31:22</ref> <bdbheb>כְּתֵפָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Chr 15:15\" b=\"13\" cBegin